    },
    "intro": "Families choose a home care agency on trust, so the name should sound calm, kind and dependable. This **Home Care Name Generator** suggests names for home care, senior care and domiciliary care agencies in six styles, including names built from your town or your own name.",
    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check a home care name is free?",
        "answer": "Press **Check** on any name to see whether it's free as a company name, a domain and a social media handle. Before you commit, search the official registers too: in the UK, Companies House; in the US, your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is home care the same as domiciliary care?",
        "answer": "Yes. <em>Domiciliary care</em> is the formal UK term for care in a person's own home, while most agencies call it <em>home care</em> or <em>care at home</em> in their name because it is clearer to families. In the US, <em>home care</em> and <em>senior care</em> are the usual words. In England a home care agency giving personal care must register with the Care Quality Commission (CQC), so check your name there too."
      }
    ]
